<title>JAPAN: France's SNCF launches 4.7% yen/US$ samurais - Daiwa.</title>
<headline>France's SNCF launches 4.7% yen/US$ samurais - Daiwa.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/U.S. dollar dual samurai issue was announced by lead manager Daiwa Securities on Tuesday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Societe Nationale des Chemins de Fer Francais</p>
<p>		     (SNCF)</p>
<p> AMT		 30 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    4.7 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  27 June 2000</p>
<p> TYPE		dual-currency samurai</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  27 Dec 1996</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	Dec 12 to Dec 26</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AAA, Moody's Aaa</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Daiwa Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Sumitomo Bank</p>
<p>NOTES: Holders will receive $4,421.65 for each 500,000-yen bond held at maturity.</p>
</text>
